														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4602938">
									

<p>I'm a bit let down, I feel that something more interesting could be done with this concept if it was executed better.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Click&nbsp;to&nbsp;see&nbsp;full&nbsp;review.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>After reading the first document, knowing what the title was, I pretty much deduced how it was going to go fairly quickly. I was hoping that maybe it'd end with an endless loop that the foundation would have to keep as a secret. I was wrong, sadly, and my second prediction, that I didn't like as much, came true.</p>
<p>I think that it's also somewhat strange that the SCP foundation would log a seemingly non-anomalous meteor as an SCP, as they did in the third document. Yes, they would most likely recognize and respond to the threat, but I'm sure there's some other form of documentation they would use.</p>
<p>And each individual document feels a little rushed, a little off. Not that they need to be much longer or anything, but it feels like it was put together hastily, like it was all written and put together by one person in an attempt to really hit you with that punch at the end. I know that it obviously <em>was</em> written all by one person, but it shouldn't <em>feel</em> that way</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

