<p>To address your concerns:</p>
<ol>
<li>That's fine if you figured out the twist too early and it's also fine that you didn't enjoy the article as a result. I try to write my stuff to be accessible to a general audience, and sometimes that means not getting super weird and esoteric with my reveals.</li>
<li>They logged it as an SCP post-hoc because it disappeared. One can safely assume that it wasn't an SCP and wasn't connected to the other two 5153 files until this happened.</li>
<li>To be fair, this <em>was</em> put together quite hastily, as it was a jamcon entry. Additionally, my preferred style in general doesn't tend to waste any time. I viewed this as a simple set up, build up, and reveal, and played it as such. That didn't work for you, but that's fine.</li>
</ol>
<p>Thanks for the read and the thoughtful comment, even if you didn't enjoy :D</p>

